      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Near-linear Dy3 cluster with weak ferromagnetic Dy–Dy coupling and slow relaxation of the magnetisation with more than one relaxation process. χT at 300 K is 42.05 emu K mol−1; it decreases to 40.2 emu K mol−1 at 20 K then rises to 58.5 emu K mol−1 at 1.8 K. Magnetisation at 1.8 K levels near 16.4 µB around 15 kOe. Arrhenius analysis of ac data gives two regimes (below/above 6 K): Δ = 28.7 K, τ0 = 6.3×10−5 s and Δ = 69.3 K, τ0 = 5.9×10−8 s. Fit of low-T χT with Ising exchange gives J_Dy–Dy = +3.9(4) K; dipolar contributions are ferromagnetic (Jdip12 = 6.8 K, Jdip13 = 6.5 K). Easy axes of the three Dy ions are essentially collinear.",
